nd wheel systems; and e-mobility solutions, as well as elevators and escalators, home appliances, air conditioners, industry and distribution solution, water and environment solutions, and industrial machinery. In addition, the company offers semiconductor manufacturing equipment; electron microscopes and atomic force microscopes; analytical systems, such as spectrophotometers, thermal analysis and chromatography systems, x-ray fluorescence analyzers, silicon drift detectors, potentiometric titrator, laser induced breakdown spectroscopy, and magnetic induction devices; clinical analyzers, and treatment and diagnostics solutions. Further, it provides automated manufacturing and robotic technologies, industrial & portable air compressors, industrial equipment systems, build-to-order industrial equipment, water environment solution, ATM and cash recycling. Hitachi, Ltd. was founded in 1910 and is headquartered in Tokyo, Japan.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Toshiaki  Tokunaga | President, CEO, Representative Executive Officer & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $3.0M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 287K people. Revenue per employee of $336K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $19K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Hitachi Ltd. is a large-cap industrials business with a $136.9B market cap on $96.7B of annual revenue.","The business throws off $5.5B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 2.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 2.0% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is 